    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This substantial 1930s three-bedroom semi-detached home extends to approximately 120.9 sq. m. (1,301 sq. ft.) excluding the garage and occupies a wonderful position directly opposite the park, with the seafront close by and sea views from the upper floor. In the same family for generations, the property has been a much-loved home and, while now requiring some modernisation, offers considerable potential for its next owners.\r\n\r\nThe house has generous proportions throughout and retains attractive original features, including two original fireplaces. The galley-style kitchen to the rear and the bathroom have both been modernised in recent years and are in very good condition. Elsewhere, the house provides plenty of scope for a new owner to update and adapt the accommodation over time.\r\n\r\nThe ground-floor accommodation comprises an entrance hall, living room, dining room and breakfast room, together with the galley kitchen, useful storage and adjoining garage. The two principal reception rooms are particularly well proportioned and retain their original fireplaces. The existing layout provides considerable flexibility, with potential to reconfigure or extend the living accommodation, subject to the necessary planning permission.\r\n\r\nUpstairs there are three bedrooms, a modernised bathroom and separate WC. The two main bedrooms are generous doubles, while the third is a comfortable single bedroom. The elevated position provides an attractive outlook, including views towards the sea from the upper floor.\r\nOutside, the property occupies a particularly wide site, with ample off-street parking to the front. There is side access as well as access through the attached garage, adding to the flexibility and future potential of the property. To the rear is a lovely enclosed garden with mature trees, providing a private and tranquil setting.\r\n\r\nThe location is undoubtedly one of the property's greatest strengths. Positioned directly opposite the park, the house enjoys an open outlook with wonderful recreational amenities immediately at hand. The seafront and promenade are within easy reach, offering coastal walks and cycle routes, while the surrounding area is well served by schools, sporting clubs, shops, cafés and restaurants. Regular bus services and convenient DART connections provide easy access to the city centre and beyond.\r\n\r\nFor anyone looking for a house they can renovate and shape to their own requirements, this property has all the important ingredients already in place: 1930s character, generous rooms, a wide site, garage, side access, ample parking, a mature enclosed garden and, above all, an outstanding position. With the kitchen and bathroom already upgraded, the house provides a very good starting point for further improvements and has the potential to become a superb long-term family home."
      },
